<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cartimandua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 43–69 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cartimandua was queen of the Brigantes of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the 1st century CE and a client ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. In 51 she handed over the fugitive British leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caratacus">Caratacus</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. Her divorce from her consort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venutius">Venutius</a> split the Brigantes, and when he rose against her in 69 Roman troops rescued her, after which the Romans conquered her kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cartimandua.jpg" alt="Cartimandua" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bartolozzi (publisher/printer; printmaker; Italian; British; Male; 1728 - 1815) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cartimandua.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
